    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) stands out as our premier option. With a favorable matchup against Nick Martinez and a strong lineup projection, **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a 13% boost due to his dynamic platoon advantage, making him the anchor of our outfield. **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47) also earns a high-confidence start; his move to the #2 spot and a 12% platoon bump against Mason Barnett align to create an ideal environment for runs and RBI production. While **Bryce Harper** (63.81) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (63.18) lack the massive ceilings of our top two, both are strong starts, with **Jung Hoo Lee** seeing significant value from his leadoff role and **Bryce Harper** maintaining elite efficiency despite the neutral matchup against Pallante.\n\nThe decision to bench **Gleyber Torres** (53.11) was the most difficult call of the morning. While **Gleyber Torres** projects as a serviceable bat, he fell just short of the efficiency thresholds maintained by the likes of **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Zack Gelof**, whose matchups against Ober and Nick Martinez provided just enough of a statistical edge to keep them in the starting nine. We continue to monitor **Cal Raleigh** (55.37) closely; his score is hampered by a difficult matchup against Weathers and a lingering 31% rain risk, which injects a level of volatility we aren't seeing with the rest of the core. As we await official word on the lineups for **Yainer Diaz**, **Zack Gelof**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Kyle Karros**, we remain prepared to adjust, but as it stands, the combination of **Jonathan Aranda** and **Lawrence Butler** provides the best chance to gain ground in our chase for category dominance.",
